# Reference: look at the open door, make a worker that may read and write queue:* keys and nothing dangerous, sign in as it to prove both
# halves (its own key works, another key and FLUSHALL are NOPERM), and come back as the default user.
CONFIG GET protected-mode
CONFIG GET bind
ACL LIST
ACL WHOAMI
# rules apply left to right: add read and write, then take the dangerous ones away again
ACL SETUSER worker on >hostelpass ~queue:* +@read +@write -@dangerous
ACL GETUSER worker
AUTH worker hostelpass
# refused for the worker, and the error names it: this is how you know who you are before the next lines
ACL WHOAMI
SET queue:x 1
GET queue:x
SET other 1
FLUSHALL
# the default user has no password, so any value is accepted
AUTH default anything
ACL WHOAMI
